Yes.  I thought it might be interesting how I tried to prepare for 
certain things and how it all did not help because my attention was only 
focused on a monster-caused death but not on a "technical one". 
Actually, I realized later that by using the "/" command, I could have 
noted that there was a drawbridge there.  Still have to verify if the 
drawbridge looks any different from ordinary floor in a color window. 
(Then I might have been warned.)

Moreover, I have left out a lot of the later boring stuff.

But I liked certain tricks that were possible in this game due to the 
early ring of polycontrol plus an early wand of polymorph (otherwise 
polymorphing into a black dragon would have cost so much energy that I 
could not have used my breath attack - I noticed this when I became a 
green dragon using the #youpoly command; I was left with 0 energy 
afterwards).  In particular, eating killer bees as a green dragon to 
become "especially healthy" seemed neat to me.  However, I realized 
later that you can eat them in any form that is not killed immediately 
by their poison.  You will lose stats, but they come back when you 
return to doppelganger form.

I *hope* I will pay more attention to drawbridges in the future! (I do 
already at the castle, at Ludios, and at Grund's stronghold, but these 
are standard situations, present in - almost - every game.)

What I noted and what seemed odd to me is that I died with 347 of 351 Hp 
left.  So I would also have died in polymorphed form.  On the other 
hand, when I was burnt by lava, my Hp went down to zero.  I would think 
that if you are hit by a chunk from a drawbridge, you should also go to 
zero, and actually you should survive if you were polymorphed before, 
because after coming back to your original form, you would not be hit by 
the chunk a second time (in lava, you should of course continue to 
burn...).  After all, those critters at the bottom of the mines (titan 
and mind flayer) came back after being *desintegrated* (here I would 
say, they should not return to their original gnomish form, 
desintegration should kill you even in polymorphed form, only the riders 
should have the possibility to reintegrate their bodies).

